== Family 1: foundational / constitutional / philosophy ==

Sources include the BITCORE Manifesto, Charter branches, Constitution, Foundational Triad, philosophical summary, and constitutional revision summary.

'''Durable signal:'''

* BITwiki is not merely a neutral encyclopedia; it has an authored intellectual and operational covenant;
* epistemic skepticism, human agency, purposeful recursion, systems thinking, composability, and the Digital Codex vision are primary design sources;
* strong language and performative/philosophical branches are intellectual lineage, not embarrassing residue;
* amendments and reconciliations must preserve prior branches and explain what changed.

'''V2 disposition: preserve + reconcile, not normalize.'''

The current [[BITwiki:Manifesto]], [[BITwiki:Charter]], [[BITwiki:Constitution]], and [[BITwiki:Foundational triad]] already provide a current canonical surface while preserving historical lineages. Historical constitutional revisions remain provenance evidence rather than alternate current policy.

== Family 2: epistemics / evidence / provenance ==

Sixteen sources cover claim validation, epistemic frameworks and tiers, evidence frameworks/tiers/evaluation, source hierarchy/types, uncertainty, provenance, audits, and performative epistemics.

'''Durable signal:'''

Knowledge should expose why a claim is believed, what its evidence is, what uncertainty remains, where it came from, how it was reviewed, and what could change its standing.

V1 repeatedly experimented with tiers, confidence fields, scalar values, evidence classes, and processual alternatives. These should not be collapsed into one score.

'''V2 disposition: mature into an inspectable evidence topology.'''

Current V2 already separates Epistemic status, confidence rationale, provenance, review/lifecycle and claim-level qualification. The remaining research question is which recurring evidence/claim structures deserve first-class properties, templates or subobjects rather than prose.

== Family 3: ontology / semantics / relationships ==

Sixteen sources cover entity types, expanded/revised variants, taxonomy, relationship catalogs/types, semantic patterns, ontology alignment, performative ontology, EPV, diagram specification, and validation rules.

'''Durable signal:'''

Knowledge is polyhierarchical, relational and facet-rich. Types are constructed lenses, relationships carry meaning, external mappings lose information, and schema should evolve from use.

'''V2 disposition: core primitive separation accepted; vocabulary remains empirical.'''

See [[BITwiki:V1 ontology maturation]]. Entity type, Domain, navigation, Book Matter, epistemics/lifecycle and Relationships remain separate primitives. Historical Topic/type/property catalogs are research evidence, not a backlog.

== Family 4: composition / templates / transclusion ==

Ten architecture sources cover Transclusion Rules, historical Infobox families, SMW Template System, Template Catalog/Usage Guide, template-system validation, and template documentation.

This family must be read together with the 52 artifacts classified as [[BITwiki:Book Matter|Book Matter]] / reusable composition.

'''Durable signal:'''

A coherent knowledge object can expose reusable parts without copying them into multiple contexts. Templates should encode repeated behavior; transclusion should preserve one canonical signal; composition should support progressive disclosure without fragmenting everything.

'''V2 disposition: Candidate, with direct implementation evidence.'''

V1's two first-class historical subject pages were assembled through transclusion, and multiple definition/method/protocol/evidence fragments used <code>&lt;onlyinclude&gt;</code> and fragment metadata. Final V2 composition rules should therefore be validated against actual caller/reuse needs, not recreated as a giant template inventory.

== Family 5: semantic schema / SMW / queries / modules ==

Thirteen sources cover page/property/event types, the Property Dictionary, citation/dependency patterns, Lua module specifications, query patterns, SMW property definitions/types/query references, and epistemic property schema.

'''Durable signal:'''

Machine-readable semantics require explicit contracts, but executable schema should be smaller and stricter than design imagination until recurring content proves the need.

'''V2 disposition: research → validated implementation.'''

Promote properties/modules only when their single job, value/target constraints, callers, and validation are known. Native MediaWiki state should not be duplicated merely because V1 proposed a property for it.

== Family 6: navigation / portals / categories / visualization ==

Four architecture sources cover category architecture, portal architecture, glossary, and knowledge-graph visualization. Nineteen additional V1 pages are classified directly as navigation/interface artifacts.

'''Durable signal:'''

There should be many views over one knowledge substrate: portals, categories, indices, semantic queries, outlines, graphs and machine-readable maps.

'''V2 disposition: Candidate.'''

Navigation must remain able to change without mutating ontological identity. A graph is a generated view over explicit semantics, not a substitute for ontology or evidence.

== Family 7: quality / governance / stewardship ==

Six sources cover governance framework/integration, quality bar/standards, stewardship and quality validation.

'''Durable signal:'''

A curated knowledge system should state authority, review expectations and quality responsibilities explicitly rather than performing decentralization it does not actually have.

'''V2 disposition: preserve explicit stewardship; separate governance from epistemic truth.'''

Governance decides who may change or steward a system. Epistemics describes support for claims. The two can interact but must not be the same field.

== Family 8: deployment / integration / migration / operations ==

Five sources cover deployment, integration, performance, user operation and content migration.

'''Durable signal:'''

A sophisticated knowledge architecture has operational constraints: deployment prerequisites, migration fidelity, performance budgets, extension dependencies and operator/user workflows.

'''V2 disposition: operational contract, not ontology.'''

These sources should pressure deployment documentation, validation and migration tooling. They should not become subject Entity types or semantic properties merely because V1 placed them in Main.

== Family 9: system architecture / boundaries ==

Four sources cover architecture overview, BITHUB boundary specification, system architecture and wiki-organization guidelines.

'''Durable signal:'''

BITwiki, BIThub and BITCORE have distinct but connected jobs. Durable semantic knowledge, live collaborative work, and cognition/orchestration should interact without collapsing into one runtime or repository.

'''V2 disposition: source-reconcile against the current ecosystem boundary.'''

See [[BITwiki:Ecosystem]], [[BITwiki:Knowledge lifecycle]], and [[BITwiki:Organization]]. Historical runtime details remain lineage; the durable boundary should not be coupled to one agent/model stack.

== Family 10: research synthesis / knowledge systems ==

The direct architecture-role corpus contains one first-order research-synthesis page, <code>Knowledge Engine Patterns</code>; V1 also has a separate Research Synthesis Index classified as navigation.

'''Durable signal:'''

External research and comparative systems should feed architectural evolution without becoming canon solely because they were synthesized by an agent or research workflow.

'''V2 disposition: provenance-bearing research input.'''

Research synthesis may generate candidates, mappings, reports and experiments. Canonicalization remains a separate review step.

== Cross-family rules ==

# '''Family is not lifecycle.''' <code>.REVISED</code>, Coraline integrations and revision summaries retain their family while carrying historical-branch flags.
# '''Family is not ontology.''' No architecture-family label belongs in <code>Entity type</code>.
# '''Historical implementation and design intent remain distinct.''' A specification is evidence of desired capability; only callers/config/runtime evidence proves implementation.
# '''Foundational voice receives special handling.''' Canonical reconciliation must not erase powerful authored formulations merely to make prose uniform.
# '''Machine behavior requires validation.''' Any property, template, module, query or relation promoted from these families needs executable tests.
# '''Current architecture can supersede a mechanism without erasing its signal.''' Retirement of V1 machinery is not deletion of V1 intellectual lineage.

== Reproducibility ==

Run:

<pre>
python scripts/validate_v2.py
python scripts/inventory_corpus.py
python scripts/classify_v1_page_roles.py
python scripts/classify_v1_architecture_families.py
</pre>

The architecture-family classifier fails if the page-role matrix no longer contains exactly 83 architecture/system pages, if a source becomes unmapped, or if the explicit mapping contains a stale title.

